Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:00:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] SystemUI: rework the AOD style animations

- Use emphasized easing for the clock's motion and stagger the fades:
  the date and battery fade first, the clock rises, shrinks and loosens
  from condensed to regular width, and the scrim only reveals the
  lockscreen once the clock has mostly left, so the stock clock under it
  never shows next to this one. Entering AOD, the content fades in once
  the scrim has covered the lockscreen.
- Stop aiming the clock at the stock clock: the lockscreen keeps its
  large clock while waking and moves it on its own afterwards.
- Glide to new burn-in offsets instead of jumping.
- Extend the scrim to the bottom indication area: the large two line
  stock clock reaches past the middle of the screen.
- Raise the style to Z 100 and hide it below a 0.01 AOD amount.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I5f32fd483b1d55a870cfbd3402d3dd7858913ebe
